{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>YHWH</b> — After He mentioned these two proofs, he said: Therefore Your name stands forever. And this name was made known to Israel alone, and by it He is called, and it shall stand, for HaShem will establish us. And if evil befalls Israel, it shall yet return as it was. Therefore —"], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 135, :notes {0 "The comment breaks off with על כן — ('Therefore —') with no completion; translated hyper-literally as it stands."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:41:46.433134629Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}